      "writtenOn": "2026-10-03T00:22:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i.e. something like this:\n\n```\nstruct PayloadBoundary {\n    size_t size;\n    bool truncated;\n};\n...\nfor (uint32_t i \u003d groupStart; i \u003c groupEnd; ++i) {\n    const bool truncated \u003d !hasCompleteNextOffset \u0026\u0026\n                           directoryResult-\u003eget_entry(i).size \u003e availableSize;\n    payloadBoundaries[i] \u003d {size, truncated};\n}\n```\n\nThen the second loop only reads `payloadBoundaries[i].truncated` and `.size`, and the `dirSize` / `availableSize` locals there go away.",
