      "side": 1,
      "message": "Metadata-only entries are now exposed as frames (`getFrameCount()` includes them). Decoding them returns `kInvalidScale`. Did you check that Blink does not mark the *whole* decoder as failed when one frame `i \u003e 0` fails? For example, `WebImage::FramesFromData` (used for favicons) iterates over all frames. Before this CL, these entries were not visible, so this is seems like a new path for Blink.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 457,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 463,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "5e93163b48d2ba121a40f0247c8a0eef63a76f8d",
